.el .ds Aq '
.TH pvc-tvfilter 1  "pvc-tvfilter " 
.SH NAME
pvc\-tvfilter \- Filter with a time\-varying .pva analysis file
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBpvc\-tvfilter\fR [\fB\-\-fft\fR] [\fB\-\-window\-size\fR] [\fB\-\-window\fR] [\fB\-\-frames\-per\-sec\fR] [\fB\-\-time\-factor\fR] [\fB\-\-pitch\fR] [\fB\-\-freq\-shift\fR] [\fB\-\-gain\fR] [\fB\-\-filter\-pitch\-mode\fR] <\fB\-\-filter\-response\fR> [\fB\-\-analysis\-channel\fR] [\fB\-\-invert\-mode\fR] [\fB\-\-time\-origin\fR] [\fB\-\-rate\fR] [\fB\-\-window\-low\fR] [\fB\-\-window\-high\fR] [\fB\-\-loop\-mode\fR] [\fB\-\-onset\-release\fR] [\fB\-\-autostop\fR] [\fB\-\-loop\-normalization\fR] [\fB\-\-loop\-smooth\fR] [\fB\-\-comp\-threshold\fR] [\fB\-\-comp\-db\fR] [\fB\-\-filter\-transpose\fR] [\fB\-\-filter\-shift\fR] [\fB\-\-filter\-release\fR] [\fB\-\-filter\-attack\fR] [\fB\-\-filter\-source\-gain\fR] [\fB\-\-filter\-warpshape\fR] [\fB\-\-filter\-smoothing\fR] [\fB\-\-shelf\-low\-gain\fR] [\fB\-\-shelf\-high\-gain\fR] [\fB\-\-shelf\-low\-freq\fR] [\fB\-\-shelf\-high\-freq\fR] [\fB\-\-frame\-norm\-limit\fR] [\fB\-\-normalize\-to\fR] [\fB\-\-attack\fR] [\fB\-\-release\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIINPUT\fR> <\fIOUTPUT\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Like `filter`, but the response is a time\-varying sequence of frames (a legacy `.pva` file) navigated over time the same way `twarp` navigates its own resynthesis source, rather than one static `.fr` file.
.PP
Ports `tvfilter`\*(Aqs audio\-processing path (`legacy/pvc_src/ tvfilter.c`); see `pvc\-core::tools::tvfilter`\*(Aqs doc comment for what\*(Aqs in and out of scope (oscillator\-bank resynthesis, and a dead `\-u` flag).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-fft\fR \fI<FFT>\fR [default: 1024]
FFT size (must be a power of two) \- independent of the filter response file\*(Aqs own FFT size (see `pvc\-core::tools::tvfilter`\*(Aqs doc comment on `N_ratio`)
.TP
\fB\-\-window\-size\fR \fI<WINDOW_SIZE>\fR [default: 0]
Analysis/resynthesis window length. `0` means auto (`2 * fft`)
.TP
\fB\-\-window\fR \fI<WINDOW>\fR [default: hamming]

.TP
\fB\-\-frames\-per\-sec\fR \fI<FRAMES_PER_SEC>\fR [default: 200]

.TP
\fB\-\-time\-factor\fR \fI<TIME_FACTOR>\fR [default: 1]
Time expansion/contraction factor (`1.0` = unchanged duration)
.TP
\fB\-\-pitch\fR \fI<PITCH>\fR [default: 0]
`\-P`: pitch transposition, in semitones \- a plain number, or `@path`
.TP
\fB\-\-freq\-shift\fR \fI<FREQ_SHIFT>\fR [default: 0]
`\-a`: frequency shift adder, in Hz \- a plain number, or `@path`
.TP
\fB\-\-gain\fR \fI<GAIN>\fR [default: 0]
`\-A`: gain in dB \- a plain number, or `@path`
.TP
\fB\-\-filter\-pitch\-mode\fR \fI<FILTER_PITCH_MODE>\fR [default: source\-only]
`\-B`: whether the filter\*(Aqs own transpose/shift compensates for `\-\-pitch`/`\-\-freq\-shift`
.TP
\fB\-\-filter\-response\fR \fI<FILTER_RESPONSE>\fR
`\-F`: path to the time\-varying filter response file \- a `.pva` analysis file, either the legacy layout (a real `pvanalysis` output) or `pvc analyze`\*(Aqs own `PVA1` format. Required
.TP
\fB\-\-analysis\-channel\fR \fI<ANALYSIS_CHANNEL>\fR [default: 0]
`\-K`: which filter\-file channel to use (`0` = pair by channel index with the input sound file)
.TP
\fB\-\-invert\-mode\fR \fI<INVERT_MODE>\fR [default: pass]
`\-q`: filtering method
.TP
\fB\-\-time\-origin\fR \fI<TIME_ORIGIN>\fR [default: 0]
`\-Q`: filter time point origin, in seconds \- a plain number, or `@path`
.TP
\fB\-\-rate\fR \fI<RATE>\fR [default: 1]
`\-Y`: filter rate multiplier \- a plain number, or `@path`
.TP
\fB\-\-window\-low\fR \fI<WINDOW_LOW>\fR [default: 0]
`\-g`: filter time window low boundary, in seconds \- a plain number, or `@path`
.TP
\fB\-\-window\-high\fR \fI<WINDOW_HIGH>\fR [default: \-1]
`\-G`: filter time window high boundary, in seconds (negative = end of the filter file) \- a plain number, or `@path`
.TP
\fB\-\-loop\-mode\fR \fI<LOOP_MODE>\fR [default: wrap]
`\-o`: sampler\-loop boundary behavior (only used outside autostop mode)
.TP
\fB\-\-onset\-release\fR
`\-r`: trigger the time window only once it\*(Aqs first entered
.TP
\fB\-\-autostop\fR
`\-d`: stop synthesis once the filter\*(Aqs time position exits its window, instead of looping
.TP
\fB\-\-loop\-normalization\fR
`\-j`: keep the filter\*(Aqs own amplitude roughly continuous across a sampler loop\*(Aqs seam
.TP
\fB\-\-loop\-smooth\fR \fI<LOOP_SMOOTH>\fR [default: 0.2]
`\-k`: peak loop\-seam smoothing time, in seconds \- a plain number, or `@path`
.TP
\fB\-\-comp\-threshold\fR \fI<COMP_THRESHOLD>\fR [default: 0]
`\-E`: filter\-spectrum compression threshold, in dB (`<= 0`) \- a plain number, or `@path`
.TP
\fB\-\-comp\-db\fR \fI<COMP_DB>\fR [default: 0]
`\-c`: filter\-spectrum decibels of compression (`<= 0`) \- a plain number, or `@path`
.TP
\fB\-\-filter\-transpose\fR \fI<FILTER_TRANSPOSE>\fR [default: 0]
`\-T`: filter response transposition, in semitones \- a plain number, or `@path`
.TP
\fB\-\-filter\-shift\fR \fI<FILTER_SHIFT>\fR [default: 0]
`\-V`: filter response shift, in Hz \- a plain number, or `@path`
.TP
\fB\-\-filter\-release\fR \fI<FILTER_RELEASE>\fR [default: 0]
`\-Z`: filter envelope release time, in seconds \- a plain number, or `@path`
.TP
\fB\-\-filter\-attack\fR \fI<FILTER_ATTACK>\fR [default: 0]
`\-z`: filter envelope attack time, in seconds \- a plain number, or `@path`
.TP
\fB\-\-filter\-source\-gain\fR \fI<FILTER_SOURCE_GAIN>\fR [default: \-96]
`\-S`: blend between the filtered signal and the dry source, in dB. `\-96` (the default) is fully filtered, `0` bypasses the filter entirely. A plain number, or `@path`
.TP
\fB\-\-filter\-warpshape\fR \fI<FILTER_WARPSHAPE>\fR [default: 0]
`\-W`: filter response warp index \- a plain number, or `@path`
.TP
\fB\-\-filter\-smoothing\fR \fI<FILTER_SMOOTHING>\fR [default: 0]
`\-f`: filter response smoothing bandwidth, in octaves (negative) or Hz (positive) \- a plain number, or `@path`
.TP
\fB\-\-shelf\-low\-gain\fR \fI<SHELF_LOW_GAIN>\fR [default: 0]
`\-H`: filter response low shelf gain, in dB \- a plain number, or `@path`
.TP
\fB\-\-shelf\-high\-gain\fR \fI<SHELF_HIGH_GAIN>\fR [default: 0]
`\-X`: filter response high shelf gain, in dB \- a plain number, or `@path`
.TP
\fB\-\-shelf\-low\-freq\fR \fI<SHELF_LOW_FREQ>\fR [default: 200]
`\-m`: filter response low shelf frequency, in Hz \- a plain number, or `@path`
.TP
\fB\-\-shelf\-high\-freq\fR \fI<SHELF_HIGH_FREQ>\fR [default: 2000]
`\-R`: filter response high shelf frequency, in Hz \- a plain number, or `@path`
.TP
\fB\-\-frame\-norm\-limit\fR \fI<FRAME_NORM_LIMIT>\fR [default: 0]
`\-n`: frame normalization decibel limit (`0` disables it) \- a plain number, or `@path`
.TP
\fB\-\-normalize\-to\fR \fI<NORMALIZE_TO_FILTER>\fR [default: input]
`\-v`: what frame normalization scales toward
.TP
\fB\-\-attack\fR \fI<ATTACK>\fR [default: 0]
`\-l`: envelope attack time, in seconds \- a plain number, or `@path`
.TP
\fB\-\-release\fR \fI<RELEASE>\fR [default: 0]
`\-L`: envelope release time, in seconds \- a plain number, or `@path`
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
<\fIINPUT\fR>

.TP
<\fIOUTPUT\fR>

